  "segment_count": 185,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 9.669,
      "end": 9.679,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone, welcome back. So today"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 9.679,
      "end": 10.549,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "we're going to take a look at"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.559,
      "end": 12.549,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "homogeneous equations with constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.559,
      "end": 14.87,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "coefficients and specifically the case"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.88,
      "end": 17.189,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "where we have real roots."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 17.199,
      "end": 19.51,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "And we'll start the problem off by"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 19.52,
      "end": 22.47,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "looking at the equation x dot dot + 8x"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 22.48,
      "end": 25.91,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "dot + 7x= z. And we're asked to find the"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 25.92,
      "end": 27.349,
      "duration": 1.429,
      "text": "general solution to this differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 27.359,
      "end": 28.95,
      "duration": 1.591,
      "text": "equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 28.96,
      "end": 31.269,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "And then we also have the question, do"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 31.279,
      "end": 33.59,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "all the solutions go to zero as t goes"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 33.6,
      "end": 35.67,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "to infinity?"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 35.68,
      "end": 37.67,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "And then for part B, we're going to take"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 37.68,
      "end": 39.67,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "a look at just the differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 39.68,
      "end": 43.19,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "y dot= ky. So this is the same equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 43.2,
      "end": 46.069,
      "duration": 2.869,
      "text": "that we've seen in uh past recitations"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 46.079,
      "end": 47.51,
      "duration": 1.431,
      "text": "and we're just going to show that we can"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 47.52,
      "end": 49.83,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "use this this method to solve this"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 49.84,
      "end": 51.67,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "differential equation and obtain the"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 51.68,
      "end": 53.51,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "same result."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 53.52,
      "end": 55.91,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And then lastly, we're asked or we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 55.92,
      "end": 59.51,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "told that we have eight roots to an"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 59.52,
      "end": 62.95,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "eighth order differential equation. -43"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 62.96,
      "end": 67.27,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "-21 0 1 2 and 3. And we're asked what is"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 67.28,
      "end": 69.51,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "the general solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 69.52,
      "end": 71.03,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "So why don't you take a moment and try"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 71.04,
      "end": 72.789,
      "duration": 1.749,
      "text": "and work these problems out and I'll be"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 72.799,
      "end": 84.149,
      "duration": 11.35,
      "text": "back in a minute."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 86.789,
      "end": 86.799,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone, welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 86.799,
      "end": 88.63,
      "duration": 1.831,
      "text": "Okay, so we're asked to find the general"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 88.64,
      "end": 93.03,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "solution to x dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 96.71,
      "end": 96.72,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "plus 8 x dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 96.72,
      "end": 100.87,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "+ 7 x = z."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 100.88,
      "end": 103.35,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "And we we see that this is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 103.36,
      "end": 105.59,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "differential equation. It's linear and"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 105.6,
      "end": 107.749,
      "duration": 2.149,
      "text": "it has constant coefficients. And"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 107.759,
      "end": 109.27,
      "duration": 1.511,
      "text": "whenever we have a differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 109.28,
      "end": 110.469,
      "duration": 1.189,
      "text": "that's linear with constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 110.479,
      "end": 112.069,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "coefficients,"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 112.079,
      "end": 114.149,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "uh, one of the standard ways to generate"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 114.159,
      "end": 116.55,
      "duration": 2.391,
      "text": "the solution is to seek what sometimes"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 116.56,
      "end": 119.67,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "mathematicians call an ansat,"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 119.68,
      "end": 122.87,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "but it's to try a solution of the form x"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 122.88,
      "end": 126.069,
      "duration": 3.189,
      "text": "is equal to a constant time e to the s"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 126.079,
      "end": 128.309,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "t."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 128.319,
      "end": 130.71,
      "duration": 2.391,
      "text": "And if we substitute a solution in of"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 130.72,
      "end": 133.03,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "this form,"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 133.04,
      "end": 135.03,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "we see that taking the second derivative"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 135.04,
      "end": 138.309,
      "duration": 3.269,
      "text": "of this uh this function pulls down two"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 138.319,
      "end": 142.869,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "s's."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 151.75,
      "end": 151.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "We have no derivatives here. And we also"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 151.76,
      "end": 153.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "have"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 153.28,
      "end": 156.229,
      "duration": 2.949,
      "text": "on each term a factor of C * E to the S"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 156.239,
      "end": 158.47,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "st."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 158.48,
      "end": 161.83,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "And we want this to be zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 161.84,
      "end": 163.75,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "So specifically"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 163.76,
      "end": 166.07,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "C E to the ST can't be zero for all"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 166.08,
      "end": 169.03,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "time. So the only way that this can hold"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 169.04,
      "end": 171.91,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "is if S^2"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 171.92,
      "end": 174.229,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "+ 8 S"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 174.239,
      "end": 177.27,
      "duration": 3.031,
      "text": "+ 7 = Z."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 177.28,
      "end": 179.27,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "So what this means is if we choose s to"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 179.28,
      "end": 181.589,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "solve this polomial"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 181.599,
      "end": 184.71,
      "duration": 3.111,
      "text": "then x= c e to the s t will be a"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 184.72,
      "end": 187.11,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "solution and this will be a solution for"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 187.12,
      "end": 189.91,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "any constant c."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 189.92,
      "end": 191.35,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "Okay. So what are the roots to this"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 191.36,
      "end": 193.67,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "differential equa or to this algebraic"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 193.68,
      "end": 200.869,
      "duration": 7.189,
      "text": "equation?"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 203.43,
      "end": 203.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Well we can factoriize it."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 203.44,
      "end": 205.11,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "The roots are going to be -7 and"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 205.12,
      "end": 211.91,
      "duration": 6.79,
      "text": "negative 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 214.229,
      "end": 214.239,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And notice how this this whole process"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 214.239,
      "end": 216.949,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "has turned a differential equation into"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 216.959,
      "end": 219.67,
      "duration": 2.711,
      "text": "a simpler algebraic equation. So if we"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 219.68,
      "end": 221.589,
      "duration": 1.909,
      "text": "can solve the algebraic equation then we"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 221.599,
      "end": 227.67,
      "duration": 6.071,
      "text": "can solve the differential equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 234.949,
      "end": 234.959,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "well we've just showed that we can take"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 234.959,
      "end": 238.309,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "any constant times e to the s t provided"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 238.319,
      "end": 242.149,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "s is equal to -1 or -7. So the general"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 242.159,
      "end": 245.83,
      "duration": 3.671,
      "text": "solution is going to be some constant c1"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 245.84,
      "end": 248.789,
      "duration": 2.949,
      "text": "* eus t"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 248.799,
      "end": 253.03,
      "duration": 4.231,
      "text": "plus c2 can be a different constant eus"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 253.04,
      "end": 255.91,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "7t."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 255.92,
      "end": 258.069,
      "duration": 2.149,
      "text": "So notice how there's two constants in"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 258.079,
      "end": 259.67,
      "duration": 1.591,
      "text": "the final solution. And the reason"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 259.68,
      "end": 261.27,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "there's two constants is because we"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 261.28,
      "end": 262.469,
      "duration": 1.189,
      "text": "started out with a second order"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 262.479,
      "end": 265.03,
      "duration": 2.551,
      "text": "differential equation. So in some sense,"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 265.04,
      "end": 266.469,
      "duration": 1.429,
      "text": "for each order of the differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 266.479,
      "end": 268.39,
      "duration": 1.911,
      "text": "equation, we always have one constant."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 268.4,
      "end": 270.31,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "It's almost as if for each time we"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 270.32,
      "end": 271.59,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "integrate, we have a constant of"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 271.6,
      "end": 273.43,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "integration. And so at the end of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 273.44,
      "end": 274.87,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "day, we have two constants in our"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 274.88,
      "end": 277.99,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "general solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 278.0,
      "end": 280.87,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "uh as part of uh part a we're also asked"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 280.88,
      "end": 282.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "for any solution to this differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 282.8,
      "end": 284.87,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "equation does the solution go to zero as"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 284.88,
      "end": 287.67,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "t goes to infinity well the general"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 287.68,
      "end": 289.749,
      "duration": 2.069,
      "text": "solution has this form so for any"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 289.759,
      "end": 292.07,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "constant c1 and c2 the solution is c1"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 292.08,
      "end": 296.55,
      "duration": 4.47,
      "text": "eus t plus c2 eus 7t and we see that no"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 296.56,
      "end": 300.07,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "matter what c1 and c2 are this term as t"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 300.08,
      "end": 303.189,
      "duration": 3.109,
      "text": "goes to infinity is multiplied by eus t"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 303.199,
      "end": 305.749,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "which goes to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 305.759,
      "end": 309.11,
      "duration": 3.351,
      "text": "and the second term also goes to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 309.12,
      "end": 311.029,
      "duration": 1.909,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 311.039,
      "end": 314.629,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "so as t goes to infinity"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 314.639,
      "end": 319.99,
      "duration": 5.351,
      "text": "both e to the minus t and e - 7t both go"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 320.0,
      "end": 322.31,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 322.32,
      "end": 325.189,
      "duration": 2.869,
      "text": "So that means that any constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 325.199,
      "end": 328.95,
      "duration": 3.751,
      "text": "* eus t plus any constant* e - 7t must"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 328.96,
      "end": 331.029,
      "duration": 2.069,
      "text": "also go to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 331.039,
      "end": 335.35,
      "duration": 4.311,
      "text": "So hence"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 339.67,
      "end": 339.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "x of t goes to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 339.68,
      "end": 344.23,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "as t goes to infinity."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 351.909,
      "end": 351.919,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we have the differential equation y dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 351.919,
      "end": 355.59,
      "duration": 3.671,
      "text": "equals negative k y."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 355.6,
      "end": 357.029,
      "duration": 1.429,
      "text": "And this is the first order linear"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 357.039,
      "end": 358.31,
      "duration": 1.271,
      "text": "differential equation with constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 358.32,
      "end": 359.83,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "coefficients."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 359.84,
      "end": 364.15,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "And we're going to use the same trick."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 364.16,
      "end": 368.629,
      "duration": 4.469,
      "text": "We let y is equal to c * e to the s t."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 368.639,
      "end": 372.07,
      "duration": 3.431,
      "text": "And we see that"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 372.08,
      "end": 374.39,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "the characteristic equation in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 374.4,
      "end": 377.67,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "it's not a polomial. It's just s"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 377.68,
      "end": 384.309,
      "duration": 6.629,
      "text": "is equal to k."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 389.83,
      "end": 389.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So we get y is equal to c e to the kt"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 389.84,
      "end": 392.15,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "is the general solution. And this is"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 392.16,
      "end": 394.87,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "exactly what we had in previous uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 394.88,
      "end": 396.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "recitations when we used for example"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 396.8,
      "end": 398.39,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "integrating factors to solve this very"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 398.4,
      "end": 400.95,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "same differential equation. So this just"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 400.96,
      "end": 402.629,
      "duration": 1.669,
      "text": "shows that we can use this the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 402.639,
      "end": 405.51,
      "duration": 2.871,
      "text": "method uh to solve first order linear"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 405.52,
      "end": 410.95,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "differential equations."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 414.469,
      "end": 414.479,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay. Now lastly, we're given eight"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 414.479,
      "end": 417.27,
      "duration": 2.791,
      "text": "roots to an eighth order differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 417.28,
      "end": 419.189,
      "duration": 1.909,
      "text": "equation. An eighth order differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 419.199,
      "end": 421.749,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "equation with constant coefficients. So"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 421.759,
      "end": 423.43,
      "duration": 1.671,
      "text": "I'll just write out the roots again. So"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 423.44,
      "end": 427.27,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "we're told the roots are"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 427.28,
      "end": 431.11,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "-4, -3,"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 431.12,
      "end": 434.71,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "-2, 1,"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 434.72,
      "end": 440.07,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "0, 1, 2, and 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 440.08,
      "end": 442.87,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "And in general the solution to an eighth"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 442.88,
      "end": 444.71,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "order differential equation whose roots"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 444.72,
      "end": 447.589,
      "duration": 2.869,
      "text": "to the characteristic polomial"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 447.599,
      "end": 452.07,
      "duration": 4.471,
      "text": "uh are -4 through 3."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 452.08,
      "end": 454.79,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "The general solution x of t is going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 454.8,
      "end": 457.909,
      "duration": 3.109,
      "text": "be a constant c1"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 457.919,
      "end": 460.07,
      "duration": 2.151,
      "text": "time e to the first the power of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 460.08,
      "end": 463.43,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "first root which will be -4t"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 463.44,
      "end": 468.39,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "text": "plus c2 eus 3t. And of course we we take"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 468.4,
      "end": 471.43,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "different constants for each term."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 471.44,
      "end": 476.55,
      "duration": 5.11,
      "text": "C3 eus 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 482.55,
      "end": 482.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "plus c4 e minus t plus c5. And now for"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 482.56,
      "end": 485.189,
      "duration": 2.629,
      "text": "this term it should be e to the 0 t. But"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 485.199,
      "end": 488.39,
      "duration": 3.191,
      "text": "e to the 0 t is just one."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 488.4,
      "end": 490.07,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "So the zero root is just going to give"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 490.08,
      "end": 492.79,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "us a constant c5."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 492.8,
      "end": 497.11,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "Then we have c6 to the t plus c7 to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 497.12,
      "end": 499.99,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "e 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 500.0,
      "end": 506.869,
      "duration": 6.869,
      "text": "and then plus c 8 e to the 3t."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 506.879,
      "end": 508.629,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "So the solution has eight terms and"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 508.639,
      "end": 511.189,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "eight constants."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 511.199,
      "end": 513.19,
      "duration": 1.991,
      "text": "And just for fun we can ask does every"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 513.2,
      "end": 514.79,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "solution to this differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 514.8,
      "end": 517.269,
      "duration": 2.469,
      "text": "go to zero as t goes to infinity? And"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 517.279,
      "end": 519.269,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "the answer is no."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 519.279,
      "end": 523.029,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "In fact, although each term with a"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 523.039,
      "end": 527.43,
      "duration": 4.391,
      "text": "negative root"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 531.75,
      "end": 531.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "does go to zero as t goes to infinity,"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 531.76,
      "end": 534.31,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "there are three terms"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 534.32,
      "end": 536.55,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "that go to positive infinity as t goes"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 536.56,
      "end": 538.63,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "to infinity. And there's one term that"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 538.64,
      "end": 541.91,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "just stays constant. So in general as t"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 541.92,
      "end": 544.949,
      "duration": 3.029,
      "text": "grows goes to infinity"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 544.959,
      "end": 547.19,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "these terms will become very large and"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 547.2,
      "end": 548.949,
      "duration": 1.749,
      "text": "won't necessarily go to zero. Well"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 548.959,
      "end": 551.91,
      "duration": 2.951,
      "text": "they'll never go to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 551.92,
      "end": 554.23,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "So I'd just like to conclude there and"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 554.24,
      "end": 557.36,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "I'll see you next time."
    }
  ],
